    VPhoneSign: drop LC_SOURCE_VERSION when the command area has no room
    
    cfw install on iOS 18.6.2 fails at the final launchd re-sign:
    
        no room for the signature load command: content starts at 3208,
        3224 bytes of commands
    
    launchd ships with only 16 bytes of header padding. inject-dylib spends
    the stripped LC_CODE_SIGNATURE slot plus that padding on the 32-byte
    LC_LOAD_WEAK_DYLIB for /vh, so when signed() rebuilds the command area
    there is nowhere left for the fresh LC_CODE_SIGNATURE.
    
    When the rebuilt area would overrun the first section, drop
    LC_SOURCE_VERSION — 16 informational bytes nothing loads — and lay the
    area out again; only fail if it still does not fit.
    
    Verified against the shipping iOS 18.6.2 (22G100) launchd: with the
    command removed, inject-dylib + sign succeed and cfw install completes
    end to end.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Co-authored-by: multica-agent <github@multica.ai>

